There's really only a couple things I've changed my opinion on.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.700
But I'll still say that James Gunn is probably one of the best if not "The Best" film maker SINGLE film maker because

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.540
The Russos are two people in the Marvel cinematic universe right now.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.240
Now there are a couple new directors that are dropping like Taika Waititi is going to be doing Thor Ragnarok later this year.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.540
We haven't seen any of his Marvel films before so you can't really judge him yet.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:53.580
But James Gunn is so good at what he does that he is now sort of  like the overseer of Marvel's cosmic universe.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.320
And if you're not already excited for Guardians 3 based on some of the post credit scenes, what they've said is that Guardians 3 is going to set up

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.900
the next ten years of Marvel cosmic films. He is the defacto living tribunal of the Marvel Universe.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.820
So there's all kinds of cosmic things that he teased that they are going to be developing, what other species we'll be seeing.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:19.500
But as I talk about some of the characters and some of the issues I had with the way it used the villains like the Sovereign.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.620
We'll talk about the current state of Marvel's cosmic races but  overall the film was amazing.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:32.200
Definitely go see it in theaters. It wasn't quite able to capture the magic of the first film, the sense of discovery because in that first film

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:41.500
Everything was new and they went super weird and in an attempt to not recycle everything very formulaicly he tried to be very different with where he took the sequel.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:47.360
Tried to keep it very self contained but  I feel like a few of those choices limited the film a little bit.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.540
And there were a couple complaints that  I had with over reliance on certain types of humor and certain bits that just went on too long.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.280
But the character work was amazing!

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.840
So comparing it to the first film the characters were much better. The villains were a little bit better too.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.260
Ronin from the first film suffered from a lot of those Marvel under developed villain problems.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.820
That's been a common problem for the MCU. They're slowly moving away from that.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.920
I think Thanos is probably going to be the best example that maybe the Black Panther villains like Kilgore

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.900
or even Michael Keaton's vulture character in Spiderman Homecoming...maybe they'll break that cycle.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.960
Because they are some Grade A actors. And Kate Blanchett is going to be an amazing villain.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.860
So Elizabeth Debicki as a Yesha was a great character but there just wasn't a whole lot of her.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.520
They teased her at the end of the movie. She's going to be a much bigger thing in Guardians 3.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.560
So I will be doing separate post credit videos later this week after everybody has a chance to see the movie because

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.060
there's a whole bunch of stuff that happens during them.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.440
Some of them are way more important than others.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.020
Especially the ones that are relevant to Yondu's character.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.680
So we'll start with Yondu. Yondu had the best arch in the film. He was the best character.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.820
And I've already said a lot about how the character found his way into the first Guardians film. It was a very round about way.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:58.180
Like he wasn't originally intended to be part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:02.820
But now he sets up this huge arch that's going to continue in other Marvel movies.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.980
So you talk about Sylvester Stallone's character in those Easter eggs.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.540
They'll continue to be big characters in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.980
They've already said that even if they don't show up in the third Guardians film they will show up in other Marvel films.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.740
You know maybe the Thor franchise just because  they're cosmic but because

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.700
there are so many unknown  questions about what kind of movies they're going to do in phase 4

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.540
and which other franchises are going to get a third or fourth movie.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.240
We just don't know which movie exactly they are going to pop up in.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.060
But talking about backstory, so that's all related to Yondu's backstory.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:38.640
They tease this grand history of the Marvel Cosmic Universe.  Alot of things that the Guardians are experiencing.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.380
The trouble that they're having inside their families. Sort of them fighting happened before with Yondu and a bunch of his friends.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:52.600
So I love the way that they weave in all this new Ego the Living Planet story to the Yondu story as well as Peter Quill's history at the same time.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:02.340
So you learn a lot about his character, the history of the Marvel Universe in celestial constructs so in that way the movie is very big while at the same time being very small.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.400
So when people say it's a small movie, the biggest complaint I've seen by far is that there's very little plot.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:14.600
That's not wrong. The characters do a lot of things but when you look at it from a bigger perspective really not a lot happens in the film.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.800
And then them meeting up with Ego the Living Planet and then the big revelation about what his story line is.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:25.880
So really that's about it. So it's not like they're teasing big infinity war stuff which I think alot of people expected

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:32.540
because Thanos was in the first movie so if there's anything that it failed to deliver on it was like big universe changing things.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:39.780
Even though I thought it did a very good job of introducing very big concepts in the Marvel Universe, we haven't learned a lot about the celestials.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.500
There was the collector that teased the infinity gems.That was a big reveal.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.060
There's not really anything on that level in this movie.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.120
There are a couple big character reveals that I thought were well used.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:58.680
Which I will explain in one of my post credit scene videos but the other big setup for the new character that you've been waiting for this whole time at the end.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.420
So major bonus points for doing all the things that you thought that they were not going to do.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:08.460
Like if you remember comic book fans complaining because hey where's Adam Warlock. Where are all these other characters?

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.900
What's going on? This looks so different from the comics.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:17.140
James Gunn has so much comic book stuff in this movie but some of it's done in such a subtle way that you'd almost miss it

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:20.180
if you weren't a huge comic book fan and looking for those things.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:26.700
And most of the problems the film has  I think are largely in due to the first film just being so magical and so fresh.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.540
Like Oh my God this looks so different from all these other Marvel films. This is amazing!

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:35.140
So the benchmark is just way too high. You can do really weird stuff and they do.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:43.540
Ego the Living Planet is so weird in the movie I love it and they are relatively true to his origin story even though technically he's not a celestial in the comics.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:47.840
He's closer to being one of the elders of the universe but usually those aren't things that I complain about.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:54.260
I didn't even think they were going to do Adam Warlock in the Marvel Cinematic Universe but now they're like Oh Yeah we are definitely going to do him after Guardians 3.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:59.700
He is totally a thing. Most of the complaints that you hear about the film this week will probably be about the humor.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:07.880
The Drax character is totally interesting but  I feel like once you get more into his back story and start talking about Moon Dragon, his daughter, I think it will get way better.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:13.960
But they definitely over rely on him for some humor that just does not land. So I totally forgive him for it.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:21.180
But I feel like the big surprise was that Baby Groot worked so well. You'd think it would be super cringy but he actually was a pretty amazing part of the film.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.040
But I will go ahead and say careful for spoilers as we get into like the last part of the video.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:32.560
I'll be a little bit more specific about the things that I liked, things I didn't like, and Vin Diesel has been teasing that you have not seen full blown Groot yet.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.240
Even though he was an adult in the first film, they're like "You have not seen GROOT unchained!"

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:47.060
So just to explain the time line a little bit, from this film to Infinity War there's going to be about 4 years that pass between the end of Guardians 2 and the beginning of Infinity War.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:54.200
So if there was any question they're just implying that Baby Groot will be full blown Groot by the time we get to Thanos Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:07:03.780
But Chris Pratt, Zoe Saldana, Dave Bautista, Karen Gillan, even Sean Gunn as Kraglin the Ravager, really all the ravagers...everybody was FANTASTIC!

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:09.180
All the performances were great. It will be a fun movie to re watch even if you know the plot.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:15.640
Like I feel like the best Marvel films are the ones that you are able to re watch multiple times because even if you know the plot

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.200
It's just so fun to watch the characters on screen.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:24.440
Robert Downey Jr has that special charisma that you just instantly forgive most of the faults in all the Iron Man films.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.460
And a lot of the same is true for Guardians of the Galaxy 2. Kurt Russell is an amazing villain in the movie.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:34.380
And even though I don't always like the movies that he is in I always like what he does in each of his movies.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.540
The trailers have not done him justice.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.540
He gets vicious in this film.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:45.240
My real big Ego complaint is in that you don't learn too much about his back story other than he has this grand plan.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:53.080
He wants to replace all of life with him. Like he's literally just terraforming the entire universe into more  Ego the Living Planet.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:58.140
But beyond that he's a little under served for someone that's so big in the cosmic sense.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:02.060
He's supposed to be a celestial in this movie. You would think that it'd be a much bigger thing.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:07.460
But James Gunn teased that they spent a lot of time setting his character up. He's an important part of the Marvel Universe.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:14.600
I suppose there are ways that he can always come back in the future as opposed to characters like Yondu who sacrificed himself Han Solo style.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:23.080
Or the original way that Harrison Ford wanted  Han Solo to die, redeeming himself while at the same time going out in a blaze of glory. A literal blaze of glory.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:31.520
There is a certain sense of disappointment in that it's  not quite as connected or overlapping with Thor Ragnarok or the other Marvel films as you would like.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:37.980
You have that certain expectations of Marvel films but I think that's also in service of trying to keep it relatively self contained.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:43.060
So even though they don't hijack this movie with a bunch of other stuff, there is this sense that something is missing

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:50.500
In that you don't see other big characters pop up in a plot based way teeing up big events that are happening next like post credit style.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.900
So yes the Grand Master does show up. So that's the connection because we will see him in that movie.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:09:01.580
It's not as big  as other post credit scenes that you have seen before like the Doctor Strange/Thor Ragnarok post credit scene.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.500
So a bit of a thumbs down on that.

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:11.780
So overall I give the film a B+ almost an A-. It just dragged down a little bit by some of the comedy that doesn't land and it really does lean on the comedy.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:17.320
So it's an amazing film. Definitely go see it. And let me know what you guys thought of it if you have.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:24.420
And then we have to talk about the special thing that is Stan Lee in this movie. So like I said it's meant to be a small movie, relatively plotless,

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:38.960
But they do really big things, introduce really big concepts. So because of the big Stan Lee twist we now have a unifying theory of the Marvel Cinematic Universe and of all Stan Lee Marvel cameos.

